{"title":"1991 AIME Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Risky)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Risky)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Hexagon\" title=\"Hexagon\">hexagon</a> is inscribed in a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Circle\" title=\"Circle\">circle</a>. Five of the sides have length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/e/87edbdda753b32453027dc7cab023c0743b6b243.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$81$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> and the sixth, denoted by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />, has length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/6/296fac336caaa4265aa24b6ecbc408a348ad7e0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$31$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Find the sum of the lengths of the three diagonals that can be drawn from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/3/eb354b27503aba806bbbaab7f892990f5a3a6547.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_{}^{}$\" width=\"13\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b56caddf0c74876a022cbb3946a4eda30b38d0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]defaultpen(fontsize(9)); pair A=expi(-pi/2-acos(475/486)), B=expi(-pi/2+acos(475/486)), C=expi(-pi/2+acos(475/486)+acos(7/18)), D=expi(-pi/2+acos(475/486)+2*acos(7/18)), E=expi(-pi/2+acos(475/486)+3*acos(7/18)), F=expi(-pi/2-acos(475/486)-acos(7/18)); draw(unitcircle);draw(A--B--C--D--E--F--A);draw(A--C..A--D..A--E); dot(A^^B^^C^^D^^E^^F); label(&quot;\\(A\\)&quot;,A,(-1,-1));label(&quot;\\(B\\)&quot;,B,(1,-1));label(&quot;\\(C\\)&quot;,C,(1,0)); label(&quot;\\(D\\)&quot;,D,(1,1));label(&quot;\\(E\\)&quot;,E,(-1,1));label(&quot;\\(F\\)&quot;,F,(-1,0)); label(&quot;31&quot;,A/2+B/2,(0.7,1));label(&quot;81&quot;,B/2+C/2,(0.45,-0.2)); label(&quot;81&quot;,C/2+D/2,(-1,-1));label(&quot;81&quot;,D/2+E/2,(0,-1)); label(&quot;81&quot;,E/2+F/2,(1,-1));label(&quot;81&quot;,F/2+A/2,(1,1)); label(&quot;\\(x\\)&quot;,A/2+C/2,(-1,1));label(&quot;\\(y\\)&quot;,A/2+D/2,(1,-1.5)); label(&quot;\\(z\\)&quot;,A/2+E/2,(1,0)); [/asy]\" width=\"668\" height=\"652\" /></center>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/7/d97ee4403b1e24148f1b28ae2be083baf5f4cf61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=AC=BF$\" width=\"115\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/c/03c43515af1c087753b00fe8825613de1565746c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=AD=BE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"116\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/a/fca2853ca123ac6e07622298b605ae28f58fbce7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z=AE=BD$\" width=\"115\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ptolemy%27s_Theorem\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Ptolemy&#39;s Theorem\">Ptolemy's Theorem</a> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/0/c601905f9d4fab39286a0df05459bcc6166bc5fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$81y+31\\cdot 81=xz$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"142\" height=\"16\" />, and Ptolemy on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/c/1ec73595b50fcaac44649121d9a0f4eb8bfb4871.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ACDF$\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/f/49f960b057d88666377f28d9b5906b16aaf6f0c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\cdot z+81^2=y^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"120\" height=\"18\" />.\nSubtracting these equations give <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/8/ca84ad5fd657f18b75f4120ee73dc3214b95c68f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y^2-81y-112\\cdot 81=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"180\" height=\"18\" />, and from this <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/6/e46c7ce6d340afa2ec21fc93774f47ac9e506867.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=144$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"61\" height=\"15\" />. Ptolemy on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/d/dad61e2885c538a9eedc7969b6639097f2e8e292.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADEF$\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/a/5ea6c8a6aa9a2439e643a801e27480f45a7193a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$81y+81^2=z^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"115\" height=\"18\" />, and from this <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/4/744e56bd6dd51a18e776e8ce0492fae0f95d6a78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z=135$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />. Finally, plugging back into the first equation gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/6/0f65a6a2ea1526068ba5abba5114d38c3034d3b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=105$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/5/7352f84b8b697f094907bdd82b12e39cc66dc1a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y+z=105+144+135=\\boxed{384}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"287\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> be the inscribed angle in each of the 5 sides of length 81, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/0/520ccfc09dd7db123b8bf3bd50abacb0f798c67a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d \\sin \\theta = 81$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"91\" height=\"14\" />. Since the inscribed angles sum to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2ca003a7da0de4994b4733e203b74ff52d42553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/c/23c35b07ff24d4783584c03222966e6705ecdd48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d \\sin 5\\theta = d \\sin (\\pi - 5\\theta) = 31$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"225\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Now consider the Chebyshev polynomials that put <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/2/5621cfe65e59bb191647481c57b257e6ec962157.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{\\sin n\\theta}{\\sin \\theta}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"51\" height=\"39\" /> in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/0/c7038458fdc92e1eb1840531bbb58b11dd5ba62e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos \\theta$\" width=\"36\" height=\"13\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/1/ec1110eb60fc3caa5743451631c49d847d239f12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{\\sin 2\\theta}{\\sin \\theta} = 2 \\cos \\theta, \\dfrac{\\sin 3\\theta}{\\sin \\theta} = 4 \\cos^2 \\theta - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"289\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/9/0892711c9ea8332d3de78733e9780f476461b8a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{\\sin 4\\theta}{\\sin \\theta} = 8 \\cos^3 \\theta - 4 \\cos \\theta, \\dfrac{\\sin 5\\theta}{\\sin \\theta} = 16 \\cos^4 \\theta - 12 \\cos^2 \\theta + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"464\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>The sum of the diagonals is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/d/b8db933a96ddbf614045211957700975bfa3d036.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d\\sin 2\\theta + d\\sin 3\\theta + d\\sin 4\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"214\" height=\"16\" />, which becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/5/c558f35d51ace02c476fca1482948dde6afba55a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(d \\sin \\theta)(8\\cos^3 \\theta + 4\\cos^2 \\theta - 2\\cos \\theta - 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"313\" height=\"21\" />, and we're given <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/7/7478b60cfb66e990132616ede1ace4a3809de718.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16 \\cos^4 \\theta - 12 \\cos^2 \\theta + 1 = \\dfrac{31}{81}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"232\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/0/c7038458fdc92e1eb1840531bbb58b11dd5ba62e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos \\theta$\" width=\"36\" height=\"13\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/5/2e52fe60d39864fb5126ca2bd5bbd5e314df4838.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16 \\cos^4 \\theta - 12 \\cos^2 \\theta + \\dfrac{9}{4} = \\dfrac{9}{4} - \\dfrac{50}{81}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"271\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/2/562e10d33bd9d16cb144d2bc98facef20defced0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(4 \\cos^2 \\theta - \\dfrac{3}{2}\\right)^2 = \\dfrac{729}{324} - \\dfrac{200}{324} = \\left(\\dfrac{23}{18}\\right)^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"316\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/8/9d8a6242fe3716d1a185800436577accb94eacb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8 \\cos^2 \\theta - 3 = \\dfrac{23}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"136\" height=\"38\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/2/ea260322f2b40aebdf7b7e8fb50fe286e470164f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\dfrac{23}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"38\" height=\"38\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/b/45b39d170ad73306847048cb33f06c726d7bbf01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8 \\cos^2 \\theta = \\dfrac{50}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"104\" height=\"38\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/1/c01872ae8fbd8c034d3083f25d77afd583b19642.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{4}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c79403759e45a2721a1dcb2a6cdc162cf3a1e0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos^2 \\theta = \\dfrac{25}{36}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"92\" height=\"38\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/c/bdcaa4457413e324bf6f232dd59d9b8df08311ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}{18}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" />, which means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/0/c7038458fdc92e1eb1840531bbb58b11dd5ba62e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos \\theta$\" width=\"36\" height=\"13\" /> must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/1/f5181c4181c7caf8f1b006f55d5d5efccb3d122e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{5}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/3/8b33d907ec1985120309152ddf04900a1af5919d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\theta &lt; \\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"55\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Now <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/0/7d04051c7fec3eabab7780c1a25590fa656e74d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(d \\sin \\theta)\\left(8\\cos^3 \\theta + 4\\cos^2 \\theta - 2\\cos \\theta - 1\\right) = 81\\left(8 \\cdot \\dfrac{125}{216} + 4 \\cdot \\dfrac{25}{36} - 2 \\cdot \\dfrac{5}{6} - 1\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"599\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/5/e25c05ecee7d377a4a256a43e6a19d4823b6eae1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= 3 \\left(8 \\cdot \\dfrac{125}{8} + 4 \\cdot \\dfrac{75}{4} - 2 \\cdot \\dfrac{45}{2} - 27\\right) = 3(125 + 75 - 45 - 27) = \\boxed{384}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"545\" height=\"45\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Risky.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Risky)\">Solution 3 (Risky)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Risky)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>This solution refers to the diagram given in Solution 1.\n</p><p>Applying Ptolemy’s Theorem to quadrilateral \\(ADEF\\), we obtain\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/6/386dcda7421056f1d227f5281f188ed2bda0ba8a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[81y + 81^2 = z^2.\\]\" width=\"119\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>Applying Ptolemy’s Theorem to quadrilateral \\(ABCF\\), we obtain\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/a/f8a5b7aa36e239b96145a5d05c67d03365980519.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[31y + 81^2 = x^2.\\]\" width=\"121\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>Since this is an AIME problem and the question asks for the sum of the lengths of the three diagonals, we may assume that all diagonal lengths are integers.\n</p><p>Rewriting the first equation,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f14ab6a9a18cafc80ca8ed2bcd4361865a0920d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[81y = z^2 - 81^2 = (z+81)(z-81).\\]\" width=\"271\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Because both \\(y\\) and \\(z\\) are integers, \\(z\\) must be a multiple of \\(9\\). Additionally, we observe that \\(y &gt; z\\), so we test the smallest such value of \\(z\\) satisfying this condition, namely \\(z = 135\\). Substituting gives\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/f/cbfbc4c62b78690ec1a28f68c837dbc1e0effe77.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y = \\frac{135^2 - 81^2}{81} = 144.\\]\" width=\"174\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>Substituting \\(y = 144\\) into the second equation,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/a/49a7a2a683fbed2bf0487f6b30fe3d2016c646f6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^2 = 31(144) + 81^2 = 11025,\\]\" width=\"222\" height=\"20\" />\nso \\(x = 105\\).\n</p><p>Finally, summing the three diagonal lengths, \\(105 + 135 + 144 = \\boxed{384}.\\)\n</p><p>~Voidling\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/DVuf-uXjfzY?t=522\">https://youtu.be/DVuf-uXjfzY?t=522</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME\" title=\"1991 AIME\">1991 AIME </a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems\" title=\"1991 AIME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1991 AIME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=1991\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1991 AIME Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1991_AIME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1991 AIME Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td 